I'm not a Knight, I'm an Elven Wizard (pretty much the only race & class
I play).  Knights do have a riding advantage, their "noble steed"
doesn't become less tame when they mount, while all other classes
decrease the tameness by one each time they mount.  Since a ki-rin (or
dragon or jabberwock) is a non-domestic creature, they start with a
tameness of 5, so non-Knights can only mount it 5 times before it would
need to be retamed, but tameness goes up one each time the pet eats,
which means a Wizard w/ Stone to Flesh & 1000+ meatballs can keep
carnivores tame for a long, long time.  Since a ki-rin isn't a
carnivore, there's no way to stop it from becoming untame if you mount
it 5 times.  I do have the Charm Monster spell, so I could retame it,
but I'd rather not have to.  As for skill, I already have it up to
basic, which is much nicer than unskilled - unskilled riders have to
unmount to pick up items, basic skilled don't.  Can't #enhance riding
any further though, but I'm not even sure what advantages the higher
skill levels give, anyway.

